/-! # The certificate remainder as a nonnegative flag-algebra element

The sweep bounded the certificate column on every seven-vertex graph.
This file turns that numeric fact into the object an SOS assembly
consumes: a nonnegative element of the flag algebra supported on the
seven-vertex classes.

A flag class is an isomorphism class, and the column value was defined
on masks, so the slack of a class is read off *some* mask representative
whose column obeys the bound. Coverage supplies one for every class, and
choice picks it. The resulting `slack7` is nonnegative by construction,
which is all a decomposition needs from it; the coefficient identity
that pins which representative was chosen is the separate expansion
step. -/

